      "body": "### What does this PR do?\n\n`hf_tokenizer` now checks that the tokenizer returned by `AutoTokenizer` encodes like the `tokenizer.json` it was loaded from and, on mismatch, loads the file as stored (`PreTrainedTokenizerFast`).\n\ntransformers 5 rebuilds some tokenizer classes (e.g. `LlamaTokenizer`) from the class recipe and ignores the pre-tokenizer stored in `tokenizer.json`. For a byte-level BPE vocabulary whose `tokenizer_config.json` names such a class, every space and newline is dropped without any error:\n\n```\n\"Solve it  step by step.\n\n\tx = 3\"  ->  \"Solveitstepbystep.x=3\"\n```\n\nPrompts, validation text and decoded responses become run-together text, and no train/rollout consistency check catches it because both sides see the same token ids. Reproduced with transformers 5.5.3, 5.12.0 and 5.17.0.\n\n### Test\n\n`tests/utils/test_hf_tokenizer_on_cpu.py`: a byte-level vocabulary filed under a generic class and under `LlamaTokenizerFast`; ids must equal the raw `tokenizers` encoding and decode back to the text. The Llama case fails without the fix.\n\n### API and Usage Example\n\nNo API change. Tokenizers that already reproduce their `tokenizer.json`, and paths without a local `tokenizer.json`, are returned unchanged.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
